Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: implement single-shot contrast autofocus on Bayer input

The MSM8998 simple pipeline needs a contrast measurement before demosaicing
and a request path to a real lens. Measure two-axis gradients on the same
green Bayer phase in the centre of each sampled frame, and send the result
with its frame number. A fixed-focus camera skips the measurement.

Use the lens driver's calibrated control range. Follow the coarse/fine
contrast search and final peak check used by libcamera's RPi autofocus.
Keep lens power until stream stop after a successful focus, and close the
device on failure. The original camera Sensor API remains usable by other
pipeline handlers.

See https://patchwork.libcamera.org/cover/28540/ for the software ISP design
discussion and src/ipa/rpi/controller/rpi/af.cpp for the contrast search.

